            <ArticleTitle>Embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma of the orbit in a 38-year-old woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma of the orbit is an extremely rare tumor in adults. A 38 year old female patient with immunohistochemically proved embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma of the right orbit is reported. The histologic types, diagnosis, management and out come of rhabdomyosarcoma is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
